From 906ad6435e7b96ca3ef1eb542e2d3f031396ad0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:26:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 58/60] ppc32: Turboshaft load/store simplification uses the
 ppc addressing configuration

mksnapshot segfaulted in the first CS-linkage builtin:

    InstructionSelectorT::GetVirtualRegister
    OperandGeneratorT::UseRegister
    VisitLoadCommon            (backend/ppc/instruction-selector-ppc.cc)
    InstructionSelectorT::VisitBlock ...
    CodeAssemblerTurboshaftCompilationJob::ExecuteJobImpl
    SetupIsolateDelegate::SetupBuiltinsInternal

VisitLoadCommon takes `OpIndex offset = load_view.index()`, which is
the Turboshaft LoadOp's OPTIONAL index as value_or_invalid(), and
hands it to UseRegister; for a load without an index that is
OpIndex::Invalid() and GetVirtualRegister indexes the virtual-register
table with it (KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS at 0x4585f294).

The ppc backend may assume every load and store carries an index
because LoadStoreSimplificationReducer, which runs in every Turboshaft
pipeline before instruction selection, folds the displacement and the
element scaling into an explicit index node for the backends without
base+index*scale+displacement addressing.  Its configuration is
selected by target macro, and the list names V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64
only; the restored 32-bit target fell through to the x64/ia32
configuration (kNeedsUntaggedBase = false, every int32 offset kept,
element_size_log2 up to 3), so the backend received loads with no
index and offsets it cannot address.  Add V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC to the
list: the ppc32 backend has the same addressing forms as ppc64
(kMode_MRI with a 16-bit displacement, kMode_MRR) and VisitLoadCommon
/ VisitStoreCommon are the unchanged upstream functions.

Why 12.4 did not need it: 12.4 carried the identical PPC64-only line,
but compiled the builtins through the TurboFan instruction-selector
adapter, where a load node always has an index input, and ran this
reducer only under the then-opt-in turboshaft_instruction_selection
flag.  13.6 selects instructions from Turboshaft exclusively, so the
reducer's configuration became load-bearing for ppc32 for the first
time.  NEW CLASS for the 13.6 cycle: target-macro lists that 12.4 also
lacked ppc32 in, but whose reachability changed with the
Turboshaft-only pipeline - the foundation commit re-admitted the
32-bit macro only where 12.4 had it.

Sweep: every directive in v8/src and v8/include outside the backend
directories that names V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 without V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC
(51 lines), each compared with 12.4's directive.  In the compiler
pipeline this is the only such gate; the instruction-selector.cc
negative lists supply generic stubs ppc32 wants, and
register-configuration.cc's SIMD128 count is irrelevant without
Simd128 support.  Outside the pipeline the remaining PPC64-only lines
are simulator, perf/gdb-jit, AIX/ELF ABI, JSPI and wasm-runtime
settings with unchanged 12.4 reachability.  Two wasm-runtime ones are
worth revisiting at the next full rebuild, not here: globals.h's
kDefaultMaxWasmCodeSpaceSizeMb (the 26-bit branch range applies to
ppc32 too, 32 MB vs the 1024 MB default) together with the
wasm-code-manager.h far-jump list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/load-store-simplification-reducer.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/load-store-simplification-reducer.h b/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/load-store-simplification-reducer.h
index 8dbde46..4fd2501 100644
--- a/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/load-store-simplification-reducer.h
+++ b/v8/src/compiler/turboshaft/load-store-simplification-reducer.h
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ struct LoadStoreSimplificationConfiguration {
   // have loads with the base + index * element_size + offset pattern.
 #if V8_TARGET_ARCH_ARM64 || V8_TARGET_ARCH_ARM || V8_TARGET_ARCH_RISCV64 ||    \
     V8_TARGET_ARCH_LOONG64 || V8_TARGET_ARCH_MIPS64 || V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC64 || \
-    V8_TARGET_ARCH_RISCV32
+    V8_TARGET_ARCH_RISCV32 || V8_TARGET_ARCH_PPC
   // As tagged loads result in modfiying the offset by -1, those loads are
   // converted into raw loads.
   static constexpr bool kNeedsUntaggedBase = true;
